        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Having prepared the bar, insert it into the tapered hole in the spindle. Make certain that the contacting surfaces are perfectly clean. Foreign matter may prevent the two tapers from seating accurately and this leads invariably to unreliable readings. It is also obvious that the two tapers must be identical. For additional information on this point, refer to Sec. 15.4.",
